WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.000
AWS now rents

00:00:01.812 --> 00:00:02.637
you a virtual

00:00:02.449 --> 00:00:03.227
iPhone

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.153
Amazon Web Services

00:00:04.965 --> 00:00:06.238
now offers virtual

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:06.992
iPhones in its

00:00:06.804 --> 00:00:07.641
cloud today

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:09.268
bringing iOS devices

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:09.941
to its device

00:00:09.752 --> 00:00:10.377
farm

00:00:10.894 --> 00:00:12.073
A virtual iPhone

00:00:11.885 --> 00:00:12.521
runs in the

00:00:12.333 --> 00:00:13.405
cloud instead of

00:00:13.217 --> 00:00:14.019
on a desk

00:00:14.102 --> 00:00:15.257
so developers can

00:00:15.069 --> 00:00:16.047
test their apps

00:00:15.859 --> 00:00:16.707
without keeping a

00:00:16.519 --> 00:00:17.344
shelf full of

00:00:17.156 --> 00:00:17.898
phones

00:00:18.422 --> 00:00:19.518
It puts iOS

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.674
testing alongside the

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:21.582
rest of Amazon's

00:00:21.394 --> 00:00:21.995
cloud

00:00:22.172 --> 00:00:23.539
where developers already

00:00:23.351 --> 00:00:24.330
run their builds

00:00:24.236 --> 00:00:25.190
and their back-end

00:00:25.002 --> 00:00:25.839
services

00:00:26.358 --> 00:00:27.372
Full story on

00:00:27.183 --> 00:00:28.079
the dashboard
